(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ch-14"] = {"441401101":[["Prototype Drive","...Gamma drive test completed. All test phases have now concluded. Compiling data—"],["Dr. Newman","The timely response rate of the Testee Unit is close to 80%... Peak reaction rate has increased by 32%... The subject has far exceeded the average results of the prototype trials."],["Dr. Newman","Even the testing framework has exceeded expectations, proving that the potential of combining the Nova-Frame with STs far exceeds our initial predictions."],["Dr. Newman","If Blair knew about these results, he'd spare no effort to expand the research program..."],["Prototype Drive","Simulation frame cooldown complete... Neural sensors disengaging... Disengaged. Hatch opening—"],["","With a cold mechanical command, the sphere device at the center of the lab slowly opens. A young man struggles to his feet and staggers out."],["","Seeing the young man's slightly pale face, Dr. Newman temporarily sets aside his worries and hurries over."],["Dr. Newman","Are you alright?"],["Kaidan (Past)","...I, uh, I'm fine, just... a bit dizzy from the swaying."],["Dr. Newman","After all, this is a specialized military cockpit without any OS assistance. For you to complete all the tests on your first attempt is already quite remarkable."],["Research Assistant","Doctor, the experiment data has been compiled. Would you like to check it again?"],["Dr. Newman","...No, there's no need to review the data. Purge it. All of it."],["Research Assistant","A-All of it? But this data isn't—"],["Dr. Newman","Just do as I say. I'll handle the Viceroy's office."],["Dr. Newman","Also, contact Mr. Harrison for me. We need to make adjustments to the Testee Unit immediately."],["Kaidan (Past)","Father?"],["Dr. Newman","Sorry, kid, this matter is very important. Rest here for a while, I'll be back soon."],["","Dr. Newman leaves in a hurry, leaving Kaidan alone in the laboratory."],["","He picks up the experiment manual on the table and has a flip through. Its contents are incomprehensible, full of complex formulas, charts and technical jargon... He somehow feels even dizzier than before."],["","Putting down the headache-inducing manual, he heads back over to the spherical cockpit for a closer look."],["Kaidan (Past)","Genesis Lab... Prototype Machine \"Ursprung\"... Testee Unit, Test Type..."],["","Noticing that the monitor on the hatch still seems to display undeleted experiment information, Kaidan leans in closer—"],["","...Who are you?"],["","Startled by the sudden voice behind him, Kaidan quickly turns his head to see that at some unknown moment a strange girl had entered the room."],["","With pink hair flowing down to her shoulders, and fine, ornate clothing, Kaidan immediately dismisses the possibility that she's an experiment participant."],["Kaidan (Past)","My name is Kaidan, Kaidan Newman. And you are...?"],["","Hearing Kaidan's self-introduction, the girl widens her eyes in surprise."],["","Newman? But I—"],["","A sudden blaring alarm drowns out the girl's voice. No matter how hard Kaidan tries to discern them, he cannot make out a single word that follows."],["","The alarm grows louder, and the scene before him gradually blurs."],["","...Wake up! Wake up, Boss! Quickly!"],["Kaidan","...Where am I?"],["Harvey","You're finally awake, Boss. Come with me to the cabin, it's not safe here!"],["","The piercing alarm jolts Kaidan awake. He quickly scans his surroundings, but only sees Harvey standing there."],["Kaidan","Harvey, what happened? Where is everyone else!?"],["Harvey","It's the UNCS Rebels! We'd just docked when they launched an attack, bombing the wharf like crazy."],["Harvey","The missiles wrecked TINA's rudder. The whole crew's in the streets, covering the dock detail."],["Kaidan","Damn, I thought we could catch a break back in West Milkhama..."],["Kaidan","You stay on the ship and protect Dr. Elise, I'll go help Dana and the others!"],["Harvey","Hey, wait, Boss—your ST isn't fully repaired yet! Boss! Boss!"],["Rebel Captain","Data comparison complete... That is indeed a GKD Parcel Service ship. Damn Vesper, they tampered with the intel!"],["Rebel Captain","Good call. Without your timely notification, we would have completely missed this haul."],["Yevgeny","Vesper's ultimate goal is to drive all forces other than Milkhaman natives off the island. They will never truly be your allies."],["Rebel Captain","And what about you, Goman? Providing weapons intel, breakout cover, and now you're even directly dispatching troops in the field—"],["Rebel Captain","Ex-leader of the Ashes—what game are you playing now?"],["Yevgeny","Identity is merely an accessory to interests. You need leverage against the new government, and I need someone to assist in recovering supplies..."],["Yevgeny","Since we both stand to benefit, I'd call this a meaningful collaboration. Wouldn't you agree?"],["Rebel Captain","Hmph. You're full of it."],["Rebel Captain","We've urgently mobilized nearly half our forces for this, so you'd better bring something real to the table."]],"441401301":[["Grant","You drop off the grid, and now you're a UNCS errand boy? What's going on with the Ashes?"],["Marcus","Errand boy? I call it a win-win cooperation, Grant. As for the Ashes..."],["Marcus","Blair is dead, the new government has taken power... In a sense, the Ashes' mission as a resistance organization has come to its natural conclusion."],["Marcus","Years of war have worn us all down. Some just wanted to return to the Union to start a new life. The rest of us are stuck finding another way to live."],["Sylvie","So you cut a deal with the Union government?"],["Marcus","That's right. The new government is providing us with supplies and helping to resettle our ex-members. In return, we undertake small-scale missions when the NDF is unavailable."],["Marcus","I know it's not a long-term solution, but it's all we've got for now."],["Kaidan","Sounds more like merc work. Perhaps you'd be better suited for a position at the GKD Parcel Service."],["Marcus","Ha, don't tempt me. If it weren't for the hundreds I'm responsible for, I'd probably already be with Harpy."],["","The two exchange a smile. This reunion with his comrade brings Kaidan a rare sense of relief."],["Kaidan","So, you mentioned you'll be teaming up with us for your next operation. Care to fill me in?"],["","Allow us to explain."],["Kaidan","...Naomi?"],["","Turning toward the voice, it is indeed the young hacker who hadn't been seen for a long time, and beside her stands an unexpected companion."],["Arnold","GKD Squad, Epiphyllum, the journalist girls—it's been a while."],["Naomi","I know you've got a lot of questions, but let's move this somewhere else. This isn't the right place for a proper convo."],["","In a temporary base near the port, the UNCS's technician team is working hard to modify and resupply the STs of Kaidan and his comrades."],["","Meanwhile, under Arnold's lead, everyone arrives at the newly constructed operation center."],["","There, he recounts the story of his capture and rescue, leaving everyone in even deeper confusion."],["Kaidan","Are you saying that your attack and escape were all part of a plan orchestrated by Vesper?"],["Erisa","I can attest to that! It was because Vesper secretly informed us of Senator Arnold's transport route that we had the opportunity to rescue him before the DL."],["Naomi","A few days back, Viceroy Rosemary went public, thanking Free Milkhama across the major networks."],["Naomi","This kind of official statement will serve as an opportunity for more people to become aware of the two distinct voices among the Milkhaman people."],["Arnold","For us, this is also an opportunity to bypass the DL and establish a good relationship with Free Milkhama."],["Elise","...Everything is going according to Phoenix's plan, isn't it?"],["Arnold","Regarding the issue of Free Milkhama, he did indeed offer the right price, but this is only a temporary alignment of interests."],["Arnold","Whether it's the UNCS, DL, or Obsidian... Vesper's ultimate goal is to drive all old powers off the island and return Milkhama to the anarchic state of the \"Gold Rush\" era."],["Arnold","On this basis, a new order led by the people of Milkhama will be reconstructed."],["Kaidan","...Sounds like a bad joke to me."],["Arnold","I once felt the same, but during my captivity, conversations with Cassha Lumiere and what I witnessed at the Vesper stronghold made me realize they truly believe it."],["Arnold","Disrupting meetings, attacking Fardan, seizing the Legacy, waging full-scale war with the DL... Vesper's recent actions are enough to prove it."],["Naomi","It's a dangerous sign. Let them keep going, they'll break Milkhama's balance and end up UNCS enemies. That's the Council's read."],["Grant","Oh, now I get it. Free Milkhama's the soft option, worth keeping close as an ally, while Vesper's the threat that needs nipping in the bud. That it?"],["Arnold","The mining rights of the Central Mines and Dr. Newman's Legacy data... Those cut right into the Union's core. We can't just sit this out."],["Arnold","The calls for military intervention within the Union are growing louder, and military forces are attempting to use this opportunity to make a comeback. If it weren't for the Madam's insistence and personal involvement, the mainland troops would have already landed on Milkhama Island."],["Erisa","Heh. Good thing you held back. Dawnstar's already publicly blaming you for Fardan. They even sent a mobile squad in advance, just waiting for you to bite."],["Naomi","But this situation won't last long. If things continue to escalate, the UNCS will definitely prioritize safeguarding its own interests in Milkhama."],["Arnold","Moreover, other forces both inside and outside the island are also keeping a close eye on this conflict."],["Arnold","The Principality of Ovett has issued a warning, stating that if the situation deteriorates, it will dispatch its Peacekeeping Force to intervene in the conflict and use force to defend the safety and rights of its citizens on the island."],["Dana","Forces from every nation converging on Milkhama.... It's practically a reenactment of the war 20 years ago."],["","Dana's words strike like a heavy hammer on everyone's hearts. Almost everyone present lost something important to the Milkhama War."],["","Even Arnold cannot help but shake his head and sigh, overcome with a wave of sorrow and helplessness."],["Arnold","The final negotiations of the Milkhama War failed to provide the Milkhaman people with a fair future, which ultimately led to today's chaotic situation."],["Arnold","To tear everything down and start anew... it's not hard to understand why Vesper would take such extreme actions."],["Arnold","However—"],["Arnold","The framework of Milkhama's order has been maintained for twenty years now, and whether Vesper acknowledges it or not, this is an undeniable fact."],["Arnold","Countless outsiders have laid down roots here, and countless new lives have been born as a result. Their destinies are now closely tied to this island."],["Arnold","We cannot stand by and watch Vesper destroy all of this. But at the same time, we must also prevent the NDF from directly intervening and causing an even greater crisis."],["","Seeing Arnold's gaze turn toward him, Kaidan instantly understands the meaning behind his words."],["Kaidan","I see... So that's why you came for us, and for the Ashes."],["Kaidan","You need a team that operates outside the UNCS to break into the central mining area and stop the showdown between Vesper and the DL."],["Grant","The hell, Arnold!? You're tossing a suicide mission at us!?"],["Grant","Sure, we've got beef with Vesper, but you can't just—"],["Naomi","Easy, Grant. We don't need you to crush Vesper completely, just find a way to stop their battle with the DL from getting out of hand. And if you can, investigate where the Legacy might be..."],["Naomi","Of course, we'll be doing our utmost to provide you with assistance. STs, weapons, intel, you name it... Whatever you need, we'll go above and beyond."],["Arnold","At the same time, I'll also be accompanying Viceroy Rosemary to Sankara for peace talks."],["Erisa","...Are you serious? Sankara's right by Vesper's mining zone, and it's already surrounded by the DL army. That place could kick off at any moment."],["Erisa","One stray bullet and West Milkhama's two leaders will disappear in an instant."],["Arnold","We've prepared ourselves for that possibility."],["Arnold","We have sent invitations for talks to Free Milkhama, the DL Oceanic Conclave, and even Vesper, and have publicly announced the meeting schedule through all channels."],["Arnold","Even the hawkish DL won't make a move against us under the watchful eyes of the world. As for Vesper, whatever choice they make, they won't launch an attack on Sankara."],["Arnold","We will do our utmost to create enough political space for your actions."],["","Sankara Refugee Settlement, Free Milkhama Intel Processing Room"],["Gabriel","You're not even going to consider it? This is a great opportunity to seek formal cooperation with the UNCS and establish an equal relationship!"],["Vesper","What the UNCS needs is absolute control over arashi ore and the entire island—this will not change due to the personal inclinations of Arnold or Rosemary."],["Vesper","Even if a temporary cooperation ensues, who can guarantee that this cooperation will last? And how do we deal with the division and erosion the superpowers' capital will inevitably lead to?"],["Vesper","Don't forget about what happened with Blair—puppet of the generals and their interests."],["Gabriel","And that's precisely why I want to join this new order, and do so peacefully—to prevent history from repeating itself!"],["Gabriel","We've been cut off from the world too long. If this continues, the Milkhaman people will become total outcasts on their own island."],["Gabriel","...You've done enough. It's time to stop."],["Vesper","Gabriel, I understand your concerns and worries, and I am grateful for the efforts that Free Milkhama has contributed."],["Vesper","If Free Milkhama decides to participate in the peace talks, we will not stop you."],["Gabriel","But—"],["Vesper","But Vesper's purpose has always been to completely shatter the existing order."],["Vesper","We will proceed with Operation Dusk as planned."]],"441402101":[["","XC 119, March 3, Refugee Settlement Area, Sankara Outskirts"],["","This road usually used only for cargo transport is now completely sealed off."],["","Accompanied by the roar of machines, the Dawnstar League Armored Forces line up and drive continuously toward the central mining area."],["","The gathered Milkhaman people can only watch from afar beyond the cordon set up by the DL soldiers."],["","*clang*—"],["","A wrench flies from somewhere and strikes an ST's hard armor, leaving no mark. The sound is drowned out completely by the thundering engines."],["","But it is still enough to light the fuse."],["Worker","This is Milkhaman soil! DLAF dogs, out of Sankara!"],["Armed Refugee","Damn straight! Who the hell gave the DL the right to close our streets and storm in with troops!?"],["","Voices of opposition spread quickly through the crowd, and the DL soldiers maintaining order are forced to fire into the air."],["DL Soldier","We are not your enemy! We're here on military assignment!"],["Armed Refugee","Military assignment? Who gave you the authority to enter the central mining area on military assignment? This is our territory!"],["Worker","Come on, everyone—let's kick them the hell out of here!"],["","Seeing a dozen angry Milkhamans approaching, the young soldier panics for a moment and instinctively aims his gun at them—"],["","At that moment, a strong and powerful hand stops him."],["Tiphys","Never point your gun at civilians."],["DL Soldier","Rear Admiral Tiphys!? But—"],["Tiphys","It's only natural for the Milkhamans to oppose us forcibly passing through Sankara for our unilateral military needs."],["Tiphys","Since the mobile unit's main force has effectively already entered the central mining area, there's no need to strictly maintain the perimeter."],["Tiphys","Move the line back, and lift the perimeter restrictions after the support group at the rear passes through."],["DL Soldier","Y-Yeah, got it!"],["Armed Refugee","Hey, is that... is that Tiphys Mill? He's still in the army?"],["","Among the crowd, a few veterans who fought in the Milkhama War seem to recognize Tiphys. The camaraderie of once fighting side by side makes them hesitate."],["","As the protest loses momentum, a new view begins to emerge."],["Civilian (Male)","Why is everyone targeting the DLAF? Isn't this Vesper's fault? If they hadn't gone crazy with the terror attacks, none of this mess would've happened..."],["Civilian (Female)","Better to let the DLAF through so they can crush the terrorists!"],["Worker","The hell you talking about? Vesper's fighting for Milkhamans—you call that terrorism?"],["Civilian (Female)","My brother ended up in hospital after the riot in Fardan, so tell me—why should I support Vesper!?"],["","The quarrel attracts more attention, and the Milkhama people gradually split into two opposing factions, leaving the DL soldiers at the barricade somewhat at a loss."],["","Seeing the quarrel on the verge of escalating into physical conflict, a stern shout makes everyone stop."],["Field","What are you all arguing about!?"],["","Field and Lorna hurry over. After nodding to Tiphys from a distance, they quickly step into the crowd and separate the two opposing groups."],["Lorna","Everyone, calm down! Let's talk this out. What's the point of turning on each other?"],["Worker","Lorna, Mr. Field, I... We can't just let this slide!"],["Field","I know you've all got your own opinions, but you're Milkhamans—argue here like this and you'll only be giving the DL a free show."],["Field","As for the DLAF entering the central mining area, Gabriel has already brought it up to Councilor Lukmund."],["","Before these words are completed, a sudden string of explosions erupts in the distance."],["Civilian (Male)","E-Explosions!? Have the DLAF and Vesper started fighting already...?"],["Worker","That noise came from the northern mining area. The DL got there already?"],["","Meanwhile, the advancing Dawnstar League Armored Forces seem to receive some order, suddenly accelerating their pace, and Tiphys leaves the scene with a stern expression."],["Refugee Squad Captain","Field, the UNCS just released a statement—apparently, a group of rebels fled into the central mining area after being defeated!"],["Field","What did you just say!?"],["Lorna","What's happening here...?"],["","Fifteen minutes after the explosions, in the northern woods of the central mining area..."],["Dana","Scan complete, no hostiles in range."],["Kaidan","Alright, time to set up the fake STs. It's all on you now, Elise."],["Elise","Give me three minutes."],["Grant","The UNCS really spares no expense, does it... these are genuine military STs, and they're just using them as disposable fake rebels..."],["Sylvie","When it comes to an operation this important, losses like that are insignificant."],["Kaidan","Sylvie, what's your status?"],["Sylvie","Hong and I laid the decoy at Point One. We're shifting to Point Two."],["Erisa","Yo, we've got some good news here—"],["Erisa","We just spotted the first Vesper scout team. They're moving straight toward the trap Sylvie set at Point One."],["Marcus","So far, so good... but do we really need to go through all this hassle? Wouldn't a straight infiltration be safer?"],["Naomi","The DL's satellites and radar are constantly monitoring the central mining area, so it's unlikely a team your size could stealth it through."],["Naomi","We raise hell and brand it the rebels' last stand, it actually creates a disturbance, and then—"],["Kaidan","If our operation fails, the UNCS will intervene under the pretext of capturing rebels."],["Naomi","That's right, but only as a last resort. No one knows what serious consequences the NDF's involvement might cause at a time like this."],["Kaidan","Don't worry, we won't let that happen."],["Elise","Decoy STs are ready."],["","With Elise's words, the autonomous STs split into three teams and quickly move in different directions."],["Elise","They will disperse and move deeper into the mining area. If they encounter enemies or take a hit, they will automatically regroup."],["Naomi","The signal masks are also flawless, not that I expected anything less of Dr. Elise."],["Naomi","However, the first step of the operation isn't complete. To fully disrupt the enemy's deployment, at least two more sets of decoys need to be set up."],["Naomi","I've already re-planned the route. Once the traps are down, regroup with me and we'll push deeper into the mines."]],"441402301":[["","As the central mining area suppression operation begins, East Milkhama's top-secret council convenes."],["","The 2,851st Online Meeting of the Dawnstar League Oceanic Conclave"],["Deputy Secretary McGonagall","The second amendment to the Expulsion Act has passed committee review and will proceed to the final vote tomorrow afternoon."],["Deputy Secretary McGonagall","Judging from the results of the preliminary intention survey, the support rate for the bill has significantly increased and should not face much resistance."],["Lukmund","Though I hear there's still a dissenting voice, a group that claims the Milkhamans' have an exclusive right to arashi ore, and even to the island itself..."],["Supreme Councilor Aldia","Just background noise."],["Supreme Councilor Aldia","Milkhama Island is merely an unclaimed land formed by sheer accident. Those so-called natives are just the early settlers and their descendants."],["Supreme Councilor Aldia","They once had countless opportunities to claim sovereignty over Milkhama, yet for a long time, all human activities on the island were limited to the non-political actions of prospectors and enterprises."],["Supreme Councilor Aldia","It wasn't until the end of the Milkhama War, when the order of united and league governance was established, that a political entity in line with international rules truly existed, and the concept of \"Milkhama citizenship\" was formed."],["Supreme Councilor Aldia","\"The natives are the masters of Milkhama Island\"... This foolish assertion has no legal basis."],["Deputy Secretary McGonagall","Moreover, after Vesper launched their terrorist attacks, the moral foundation of this viewpoint has already been shaken."],["Deputy Secretary McGonagall","As long as we successfully eliminate this group of terrorists and demonstrate to all parties that we still have the ability to maintain stable order, the initiative will always be in our hands."],["Lukmund","Regarding this, the Milkhama Defense Force has already mobilized armored units to launch an attack on the central mining area."],["Lukmund","For them, this operation is also a good opportunity to collect combat data for the PAMS System, so they will surely not be negligent."],["Supreme Councilor Lawrence","Hmph, the Defense Force... Their enthusiasm lies not just in combat data, but also in using this opportunity to prove the value of the military in peacetime and gain political prestige."],["Supreme Councilor Lawrence","Those old-timers in the military have long been seeking a legitimate way to break free from the control of the Oceanic Conclave, and this time they clearly hold the same purpose."],["Supreme Councilor Lawrence","If the frontline battles do not go well, they will deploy their main forces to the island under the guise of supporting counter-terrorism operations, bypassing the existing oversight system to some extent."],["Supreme Councilor Lawrence","In hindsight, having Matilda Rossi and her adjutant take leave on Milkhama might have been a deliberate move by the military."],["Supreme Councilor Lawrence","You must proceed with caution, Councilor Lukmund. We do not want Milkhama Island to become a crack in the established order."],["Lukmund","I fully understand your concerns and have prepared corresponding plans for this—"],["Lukmund","I hope the Oceanic Conclave can temporarily grant me several privileges."],["","Central Mining Area, Vesper Base"],["Vesper Technician","Final adjustments have been made to devices 1 to 7. They are ready to launch at any time."],["Vesper Technician","Devices No. 8, 11, and 12 have also been charged up to 30% and are expected to be operational in twenty minutes."],["Vesper","Thank you for your hard work, you've done very well."],["Vesper","Transfer authority to Cassha and Lorenzo. The frontline situation is constantly changing, so let them decide the timing of the launch themselves."],["Vesper Technician","Got it!"],["","The Vesper Technician, having received his orders, hurries away with pre-battle euphoria, leaving the vast command room with only Vesper."],["Vesper","Thank you for your cooperation, Dr. Newman."],["","With this seemingly self-directed gratitude, a translucent figure suddenly appears beside Vesper."],["Dr. Newman","I just made some corrections to your basic design. You should thank young Arthur for realizing it in such a short time."],["Dr. Newman","...But to be perfectly honest, it's hard to predict how effective they will be against the prepared Dawnstar League Armored Forces."],["Dr. Newman","Perhaps it has only increased your odds from 0% to 1%."],["","Dr. Newman's face is a mix of concern and questioning seriousness, enough to make even Vesper momentarily forget this is only a Legacy projection."],["Vesper","Even a 1% chance means the impossible has become possible... For the Milkhaman people, this change is everything."],["Vesper","And also—"],["","His gaze passes through the command room window toward the giant figure standing in the hangar's depths."],["","The machinists are busily conducting the final armament setup and debugging."],["Vesper","I don't believe our odds are really only 1%."]],"441403101":[["Naomi","GKD, you're approaching an abandoned ore processing station. It overlaps with Erisa's route—rendezvous there."],["Naomi","But at your current speed, you'll lose cloud cover on entry. There's a chance DL eyes will be locked on you."],["Naomi","Punch through now to Vesper HQ, or wait for cloud cover to return—what's your choice?"],["Dana","Ahead is the mining area's center, close to the DLAF-Vesper front. Once exposed, we risk fire from both sides."],["Marcus","But since we've already tangled with Hardaway, the DL likely has our general track. Delaying could be dangerous."],["Grant","There's a strong argument each way. What's the play, Boss?"],["Kaidan","...This isn't our home turf. No matter how we maneuver, the terrain's not on our side."],["Naomi","Okay! Then I'll plot the shortest route for you—kzzzt—"],["Dana","Naomi? Your comm sounds off."],["Naomi","Really? I'm receiving you just fi—kzzzt here."],["Elise","Wait a minute, this is..."],["Elise","Sensors have detected an abnormally strong electromagnetic signal!"],["Elise","Multiple strong directional EMPs are spreading out from the central mining area to the south!"],["Naomi","What!? Everyone—kzzzt—shut down your STs—kzzzt—"],["Grant","EMPs!? Shutting down won't do jack!"],["Marcus","No, the UNCS added special electromagnetic shielding to our STs. As long as it's not a direct hit, we can ride it out from here!"],["Kaidan","There's no other choice, everyone—emergency shutdown!"],["","At Kaidan's command, everyone powers down their ST systems. The cockpits fall into a rare darkness, then complete silence."],["","Ten seconds, thirty, a minute... no one knows how long. Only when Kaidan cautiously reactivates his external sensors is it confirmed the danger has passed."],["","On reboot, everyone checks their STs. As Marcus predicted, no major damage is found."],["Kaidan","Naomi, do you read me?"],["Naomi","Bzzt... Bzzzzzzt..."],["","However, the electromagnetic interference persists, making long-distance communication with Naomi and the others unlikely to recover soon."],["Grant","What was that just now...?"],["Elise","...It's the Legacy."],["Elise","Before the EMP went off, I detected a very brief activation signal from the Legacy."],["Marcus","The Legacy's in Vesper's possession, right? How did a terrorist organization get their hands on tech like this?"],["Elise","...So this is Phoenix's plan."],["Kaidan","In any case, staying here is too dangerous. Who knows if another EMP's heading our way."],["Kaidan","If that last strike hit the Defense Force, then now... might be our best chance to break through."]],"441403301":[["Grant","Is this really a mine? Why does it look like a military base?"],["Marcus","It's not exactly surprising. The first thing we Ashes do after occupying a place is fortify it."],["Grant","That can't be it. Judging by the wear and tear on the walls and floors, it doesn't look like this place was built recently. I'd estimate it's been here for twenty, maybe thirty years."],["","They observe the surroundings while maintaining their speed through the passage."],["Elise","Heads up! Multiple heat signatures detected in the area ahead!"],["","Hearing Elise's warning, everyone stops almost simultaneously, regrouping into a cautious formation as they advance."],["Kaidan","On my mark... three, two, one—move!"],["","They split up smoothly, weapons up, aiming ahead and bracing for combat."],["Kaidan","What the..."],["","No ambush awaits them—they are greeted only by a field of wreckage."],["","Self-defense turrets, Puppets... From the scattered sparks and rising black smoke, it can be seen that they were just destroyed not long ago."],["Dana","These are Vesper's automated defenses... Looks like a squadron's worth, yet they were destroyed so easily."],["Grant","Bet it was that \"Tranquilizer\"... What sick bastard thought up that name for a slaughterhouse on legs?"],["Marcus","On the bright side, at least we don't have to deal with this pile of defenses."],["Kaidan","But beyond this point, nothing's certain."],["Kaidan","Worst case, we're up against Tranquilizer and Vesper at the same time... so be ready."],["","Sankara Refugee Settlement, Free Milkhama Intel Processing Room"],["Gabriel","How long until power is restored to the northwest district?"],["Worker Yak","It was outside the EMP's kill range, but the base stations and wiring there were already old. Most of it's fried now."],["Worker Yak","We need to replace the hardware on all major lines... It'll take at least twelve hours!"],["Gabriel","...I understand. I'll immediately dispatch electricians and engineering vehicles from the southern district to support you. Just get the grid back online as fast as you can."],["Gabriel","I've already sent Lorna with a team to transfer critical patients from the hospital affected by the power outage, so you don't need to worry about your daughter, Yak."],["Worker Yak","Thank you, boss, really... Thank you!"],["","Putting down the phone, Gabriel cannot help but sigh. The continuous toil and worry has made his chronic headache worse."],["Gabriel","Vesper... How much do you truly understand the cost of this \"transformation\"?"],["","He picks up the medicine bottle beside him, only to remember that the painkillers inside are already all gone. All he can do is close his eyes and rub his brow, hoping for some relief."],["","In twenty minutes, the UNCS viceroy's plane will arrive in Sankara. Gabriel has to pull himself together."],["","*knock, knock...*"],["","The sudden sound of knocking instinctively makes him sit up straight."],["Gabriel","Come in."],["Girl","Papa! Let's play!"],["Gabriel","Myra? What are you doing here?"],["","Despite his surprise, a gentle smile unconsciously appears on Gabriel's face."],["Girl","This lady brought me here!"],["","Only then does Gabriel notice the shadow behind her. The moment he sees who it is, his smile vanishes."],["Ma'at","Long time no see, Commander Gabriel."],["Gabriel","...Ma'at Sharif."],["Girl","Ma'am, you said someone went to pick up Mom. When will she be here?"],["","Ma'at strokes Myra's head, a flicker of pity in her eyes that vanishes as fast as it comes."],["Ma'at","That might depend on your father's willingness to cooperate."],["Gabriel","Have you really sunk this low!?"],["Ma'at","...We just don't want Free Milkhama to form any unfortunate agreements with the UNCS or Vesper."],["Ma'at","Play it our way, and everything you need is yours, instantly."],["Ma'at","Whether it's scarce materials and manpower in Sankara, or... the private flight you've been seeking to safely evacuate your family from the island."]],"441404101":[["","Sankara Refugee Settlement, Central Temporary Airport"],["","A large UNCS military aircraft slowly lands on the runway."],["","As the gangway is positioned, the hatch opens, and Shin Sagara is the first to jump off the plane."],["","He scans the guards and bystanders with sharp eyes, then signals back into the plane once it looks safe."],["","Then, under the watchful eyes of the Milkhamans, Rosemary and Arnold disembark from the plane one after the other."],["Milkhaman Civilian","Two Viceroys of West Milkhama, past and present. It's the first time I've seen so many bigwigs in person."],["Milkhaman Civilian","What exactly are they gonna discuss with old Gabriel?"],["","Field and the reception staff waiting nearby hurry forward to greet them."],["Field","We've been expecting you, Viceroy Rosemary, Senator Arnold."],["Field","I apologize, but Gabriel couldn't be here due to an unexpected matter. He sent me to welcome you on his behalf."],["Rosemary","That's perfectly fine, Mr. Adams. We fully understand the difficult situation in Sankara."],["Arnold","We are here to offer whatever assistance we can to Free Milkhama."],["Field","Thank you both for your understanding. Please follow me, we've arranged a special vehicle to take you to the venue."],["Chauffeur","Please, this way."],["","Rosemary's gaze lingers briefly on the driver, then catches a subtle sign she knows by heart."],["Rosemary","Forgive me, legs aren't what they used to be. Would you mind lending me your arm, driver?"],["Chauffeur","Of course, Viceroy. It would be my pleasure."],["","Field looks as though he has something to say, but seeing Rosemary walk on the driver's arm, he falls in with Arnold and follows."],["Rosemary","What's going on, Anderson?"],["","In barely audible whispers, the two exchange words."],["Chauffeur","About an hour ago, I discovered traces of DL agent activity in Sankara. They have likely infiltrated the venue inside and out."],["Chauffeur","Gabriel's movements are also somewhat unusual... That puts you in the crosshairs."],["Rosemary","Even so, the peace talks will proceed as planned. We must use this chance to establish a stable position."],["Chauffeur","You don't seem too worried."],["Rosemary","West Milkhama is an interesting place, and we've gained far more leverage than we imagined."],["Chauffeur","...You're still the same as ever."],["","As the special vehicle approaches, their conversation comes to an end."],["","Anderson, disguised as a driver, steps forward and opens the car door."],["Chauffeur","Climb in, Viceroy Rosemary, Senator Arnold. I will ensure both of you arrive safely at the venue."],["","Meanwhile, in the central mining area, deep within Vesper's underground base..."],["Marcus","How long have we been walking?"],["Dana","It's been almost thirty minutes since we entered the mine."],["Grant","I thought the underground facility in Fardan was bad enough, but this place is just too much."],["Grant","No wonder Vesper chose this place as their base of operations. With the automated defense systems set up along the way, under normal circumstances, few could ever reach this far."],["Kaidan","That's true under normal circumstances, but it's a whole lot different when you factor in that Tranquilizer."],["Kaidan","Dr. Elise, how much do you know about that thing?"],["Elise","Without specialized scanning equipment, the data we've collected is very limited. It can only be roughly determined that its entire body is made of a large amount of arashium alloy and has special functions to weaken the power of conventional weapons."],["Elise","Judging from its ability to accurately neutralize EMPs, it possesses computational power far beyond that of ordinary ST systems and is likely equipped with a high-spec Bionic Intelligence Frame."],["Kaidan","A Bionic Intelligence Frame..."],["","The spherical computer \"Legacy\" and the projected image of Dr. Newman flash through Kaidan's mind."],["","Nowadays, it's hard for him not to associate the term \"Bionic Intelligence Frame\" with that terrifying device."],["","Through the communication window, Elise's expression also hangs heavy, though her concerns lie elsewhere."],["Elise","If that's really the case, then the Legacy itself could be deemed the most powerful weapon of all—"],["","She doesn't get a chance to finish. Suddenly a blast rips through the passage with a wave of heat, nearly knocking Grant off his feet."],["","Even the surrounding walls shake slightly, splitting open with several cracks."],["Grant","Wh-What was that noise!?"],["Dana","Signs of battle detected ahead! It's the Tranquilizer and Vesper!"],["Kaidan","Finally caught up, huh...!"],["Kaidan","Everyone, get ready to engage!"]],"441404301":[["Dr. Newman","All pulse devices pre-charged."],["Dr. Newman","As long as they can be successfully delivered to the target location and connected to the pre-set repeater, you can shake the very foundations of the DL as you wish."],["Vesper","Operation Dusk has finally reached its most critical step..."],["Dr. Newman","...Your hand is trembling."],["Vesper","I'm an ordinary person, not a machine—just flesh and blood. I get nervous, but I will never let nerves be the cause of my failure."],["Vesper","As long as I bear the name of \"Vesper,\" I must complete my mission."],["","Phoenix operates his ST, wandering through the passage at speed toward the planned location, tapping the screen repeatedly to adjust parameters not yet optimized."],["","Suppressing Tranquilizer consumed all of the base's power and processing, causing progress to lag behind. Now he must rely on his own efforts to make up for it as much as possible."],["","He feels his nerves winding tighter. To ease the strain, he throws a long-buried question at his only companion."],["Vesper","And what about you, Dr. Newman?"],["Vesper","You bear Walter Newman's will, yet never refuse to help us. What are your considerations?"],["Dr. Newman","Is this a simple question, or a veiled threat?"],["Vesper","That depends on what you choose to believe."],["","After a brief silence, the hologram of Dr. Newman responds."],["Dr. Newman","First, let me be clear... I am not the real Walter Newman."],["Dr. Newman","This is not a difference in terms of physical form, but rather a... spiritual difference."],["Vesper","...I never thought I would hear such sentimental words from an AI."],["Dr. Newman","This is a unique aspect of the Bionic Intelligence Frame developed by your sister. Even though I do not consider myself human, I can still maintain a stable and independent personality."],["Dr. Newman","What the world saw as Dr. Newman's \"death\" meant \"birth\" to me, which fundamentally determines our different perspectives on certain issues."],["Dr. Newman","War and peace, progress and ethics, personal feelings and the greater good... The answer I choose is not entirely consistent with the Dr. Newman in my memory."],["Dr. Newman","He would hesitate because of the \"process,\" while I hope to see a different \"result.\""],["Vesper","Even if this action leads to the destruction of the Legacy?"],["Dr. Newman","...Correct."],["","Faced with this calm and unwavering response, it is the questioner's turn to fall into silence."],["Dr. Newman","The DL's conspiracy, the restraint of the UNCS, the Vesper counterattack, and... the pursuit of Kaidan."],["Dr. Newman","No matter who ultimately succeeds or fails, a new answer will be revealed."],["Dr. Newman","I want to know what kind of change it will bring to Milkhama and to myself."]],"441405101":[["","XC 119, March 3, 16:00, Southern Central Mining Area, DL Operations Command Center"],["DLAF Comms Officer","The guerrilla squad has successfully destroyed five large electromagnetic pulse generators, and the control and communication of the STs in various units are gradually being restored."],["Tiphys","Alright, have the 3rd Mobile Squad on the left flank retreat. Their line's too deep, Vesper could surround them."],["Tiphys","Gunport Group Six, conduct a half-battalion ranged attack on area W32, the enemy's retreat point. It's covered by fog, and likely lain with ambushes or landmines."],["DLAF Comms Officer","Understood! Also, Rear Admiral... according to the frontline report, uh..."],["DLAF Comms Officer","Some of the soldiers claim that among the invading forces coming from the north of the mining area, they detected a signal from Dr. Elise's ST..."],["","The hand moving on the map stops."],["Tiphys","...Where is she?"],["DLAF Comms Officer","Broke through Major Matilda's vanguard with the invaders and entered Vesper's underground stronghold."],["Tiphys","......"],["","As Elise's father, he naturally knows her well."],["","He knows that his daughter has no personal vendetta against Vesper. He does not believe her actions are due to the influence of UNCS spies."],["","The only thing that could make her uncharacteristically venture deep into the battlefield is that member of their family who remains unreachable to them."],["Tiphys","Phoenix... could it be that you really..."],["","Tiphys unintentionally glances at the watch on his left wrist, a gift from Phoenix on his 50th birthday five years ago."],["","For some reason, the watch that was functioning normally earlier is now running significantly ahead of time."],["DLAF Comms Officer","...Rear Admiral?"],["","The communications officer instinctively calls out to probe, but receives no response."],["","After a few seconds of silence, Tiphys resumes operating the tactical map board."],["Tiphys","Continue reporting the frontline situation."],["Tiphys","The most important thing now is to ensure the success of the operation and minimize troop casualties as much as possible."],["DLAF Comms Officer","Rear Admiral, Dr. Elise, she..."],["Tiphys","...Even to verify the authenticity of the intelligence, we must first attack the Vesper stronghold and catch up with the invading forces."],["Tiphys","For this reason, it is even more important we prioritize the smooth advancement of the frontline troops."],["DLAF Comms Officer","Y-Yeah, got it!"],["","With his superior's assurance, the comms officer has no reason to dwell on it. He pushes aside his concerns, throwing himself back into the mission."],["","The command center returns to its busy state as if nothing has transpired."],["","At the same time, deep within the Vesper base..."],["Grant","The deeper we go, the older this place looks... Hey, look at that transporter—what an antique! Wasn't that model phased out over a decade ago?"],["Grant","No doubt about it—Vesper didn't build this place anytime recently."],["Elise","The lighting and ventilation systems here show an activation time of XC 95... 24 years ago."],["Marcus","Wait—wasn't the central lode confirmed only about ten years ago? Why's this place older?"],["Kaidan","...It looks like the Milkhamans found the Central Mines long before the superpowers did."],["Kaidan","They were well aware that arashi ore was the root of all conflict on the island, so they kept it secret and built an underground base."],["Dana","It wasn't until three years later, in XC 98, that the DLAF landed on the island and clashed with the UNCS, leading to the breakout of the Milkhama War."],["Dana","Years after the war ended, with east and west split, the Central Mines were finally surveyed. That's when the UNCS realized the vein distribution put them at a major disadvantage."],["Grant","It's no wonder hawks like Blair still held significant power after the war and harbored such animosity toward the Milkhamans."],["Kaidan","The central mining area was the starting point of the Milkhaman resistance, which is why Vesper chose it as their base of operations..."],["","*beep*"],["","The high-frequency radar finally picks up a clear, familiar signal."],["Kaidan","It's Phoenix. We've finally caught up with him!"]],"441405301":[["Vesper","Lorenzo, what's the situation on the front?"],["Lorenzo","It's bad. The DLAF has already destroyed most of the pulse devices and is steadily advancing the line under gunport cover. They've also dispatched special units to continuously claw away at our defenses from both sides of the mining area."],["Lorenzo","Cassha's fighting while falling back. Luckily, GKD's tangled with DL units, giving us some breathing space."],["Lorenzo","But it won't last long. Soon we'll lose all room to maneuver."],["Vesper","...Twenty minutes."],["Vesper","Hold on for twenty more minutes, and I can destroy the DLAF's command system."],["Lorenzo","What are you thinking?"],["Vesper","To the southwest, there's an abandoned signal tower that used to be the control center for Free Milkhama's automated mining systems."],["Vesper","I can use it to emit a powerful temporary signal to prematurely activate the pulse device on the Fardan-bound train, striking the DLAF command HQ from the rear."],["","*beep*"],["","One-way communication line connected. Executing Security Protocol 56."],["Vesper","Commander Gabriel, Operation Dusk will be executed ahead of schedule."],["Vesper","...If possible, please arrange for the evacuation of the southern residents of Sankara immediately."],["","End of communication, records will be erased in ten seconds."],["Gabriel","..."],["Gabriel","...Well, you heard it."],["Ma'at","Loud and clear."],["Ma'at","From now on, security maintenance forces will fully assist in rebuilding Sankara. Your family will take the 8 PM flight to the capital, a million miles away from Milkhama's troubles."],["Ma'at","...There's no reason to beat yourself up, Gabriel. You made the right call."],["Ma'at","Thanks to you, the Milkhaman people have received an invitation to a new future."]],"441406101":[["Marcus","So that's what's going on... Hold tight. I just cleared the Vesper units blocking the road. I'm on my way right to you!"],["Hong","Sylvie and I are still—watch your nine... Nice!"],["Hong","Sorry, we're still skirmishing with the DL flankers here. These guys are all real elites... It's almost impossible to shake them off!"],["Dana","We still can't reach Erisa and the others. They seem to still be in the central part of the mine where the electromagnetic interference is strongest."],["Kaidan","Looks like we're the only ones left who can stop Phoenix... Grant, can you still track his signal?"],["Grant","Moving southwest, not too fast."],["Grant","Don't sweat it. Vesper's forces bought him a few minutes, but his ST's banged up. We'll reel him in."],["Kaidan","The question now is whether there's anything else waiting to blindside us along the way..."],["Elise","Steel Trooper detected! DL signal ahead, on the right!"],["Kaidan","Damn, speak of the devil... Activate the concealment system stat—keep your distance, and don't let them spot us!"],["","Fortunately, the four machines had undergone extensive modifications within UNCS territory. They successfully conceal themselves, remaining outside DL ST detection range."],["","After moving a certain distance, they realize something is amiss."],["Elise","...An increasing number of ST signals are converging. They're all moving toward the southwest."],["Dana","Could it be that the DL is already on to Phoenix's plan?"],["Kaidan","...Let's speed up. I have a bad feeling about this."],["","Phoenix pilots the heavily damaged Apophis to the target signal tower."],["","As expected, this place is far from the battlefield—abandoned, with no sign of friend or foe."],["","After connecting the Legacy to the signal tower, Phoenix leaves the ST and heads to the central control room to make the final preparations for activation."],["Vesper","The main line has indeed been severed... Fortunately, the backup underground generator is still usable, and with Apophis's auxiliary power, it can provide the juice needed for a single signal launch."],["Vesper","I've already imported the preset parameters into the system. The specific adjustments are up to you, Doctor."],["","However, there is no response."],["","Even in the battles against Kaidan, the Legacy never faltered, yet now it falls into an unusual silence."],["Vesper","...Dr. Newman?"],["Dr. Newman","Receiving priority command... Resetting activation parameters."],["","The response is mechanical, emotionless... as if returning to the state before neural encryption was lifted."],["Vesper","The activation coordinates and timing of the pulse device have been rewritten!? Stop!"],["","Detecting an anomaly in the Legacy, Phoenix decisively cuts off its power unit, forcing it into a protective sleep state."],["Vesper","Is this... a backdoor program? No, it's some kind of top-level command, even surpassing the Legacy's own will."],["","I suppose it's not surprising. The Legacy is merely a man-made machine and naturally cannot defy its true master."],["","A sudden, unsettling noise arises from behind—this time not comms static, but an all-too-real sound, echoing in the space around him."],["","With almost no hesitation, Phoenix draws his gun. He turns around and fires several shots, diving into cover."],["QRF Soldier","Ugh…"],["","A figure falls to the ground. But then six fully armed soldiers emerge from the shadows, quickly spreading out and aiming their weapons at him."],["","Then, a lavishly dressed man slowly approaches under the cover of several tactical shields... This man is not unfamiliar to Phoenix."],["Vesper","Lukmund Erambard...!"],["Lukmund","This is the first time we've met face to face, Vesper, or should I say, Lieutenant Phoenix Mill."],["Vesper","How do you know about this place...? No, it was Gabriel who told you, wasn't it?"],["Lukmund","He simply made a choice that was more suitable for the Milkhaman people."],["Lukmund","In fact, from the moment you refused to hand over the Legacy, you were doomed to fail."],["Vesper","...So it was you? The one directing Ma'at to back Vesper all this time—you, the East Milkhama governor?"],["Lukmund","I'm a Milkhaman too. I hate the DL just like you. I hate those shortsighted officials entrenched in power—I hate the so-called balance that has been rotting away since the Milkhama War."],["Vesper","You what...!?"],["Lukmund","But at the same time, I also despise the Milkhamans who live passively without resistance, and the Sankarans who possess the central mining area yet fail to utilize it—it's all nauseating to me."],["Lukmund","That's why I returned to Milkhama. Seventeen years I spent climbing the ranks, all the way from secretary to governor. I contacted Dr. Newman, supported Elise's research team—all to gain the strength necessary to alter the status quo."],["Lukmund","But all of this ultimately cannot escape the limitations of the existing framework. For true change, there must be an \"external enemy\" capable of shaking the foundations of order."],["Lukmund","It was at this moment that Vesper appeared. A fearless native rebel with a clear cause—there could be no better catalyst."],["","Despite the murderous stare almost overflowing from his eyes, Phoenix remains hidden behind cover, staying vigilant without revealing the slightest weakness."],["Lukmund","Assassinating high-ranking officials, opposing the army, intensifying the conflict between the Milkhamans and the DL... you have achieved all of these so well, far beyond my expectations."],["Lukmund","You even managed to find Kaidan's prototype data before anyone else, discovering a way to unlock the Legacy, and thus making the self-improvement of the Bionic Intelligence Frame possible."],["Lukmund","The next steps became quite simple—introduce you to the Legacy, to Kaidan, and allow you to seize power on my behalf."],["Lukmund","The Oceanic Conclave also re-evaluated the situation in Milkhama due to your antics, investing more resources to serve my interests."],["","The rapid-response team's footsteps draw near. Phoenix tries to grasp the situation, but in the next instant, a dense barrage of gunfire pushes him back."],["Lukmund","And now, as long as your pulse weapon detonates in the \"right place,\" the DLAF will become the enemy of the people, with no standing left to resist me."],["Lukmund","In comparison, the chaos, civilian deaths, and political disgrace... these temporary losses can hardly be called a cost."],["Vesper","All this blood, just to fuel your political ambition?"],["Lukmund","This is not necessarily a bad thing for the Milkhaman people."],["Lukmund","The mutual destruction of the DLAF and Vesper will force the mainland to reassess the dangers of the Expulsion Act, and Free Milkhama will gain greater recognition through cooperating with us."],["Lukmund","The Milkhaman people can retain their citizenship and live and work peacefully on this island... I will realize the future you've been fighting for."],["Lukmund","It's over for you, Vesper."],["","The rapid response team approaches Phoenix's location. In a matter of seconds, the entire team's crosshairs will be on him."],["Vesper","...As long as there are people like you on the island, my mission will never be over."],["","With a thunderous crash, a steel hand punches through the wall, hurling the unprepared DL troops away."],["","Phoenix seizes the moment. Crouching low and sprinting out into the open, he uses the ST's arm for cover and he leaps through the breach."],["QRF Soldier","Fire! Don't let him escape!"],["","A few beats late, dense gunfire erupts, but only a few bullets graze Phoenix's clothing."],["","The rapid response team raises their weapons at the breach, only to see the cockpit closing quickly."],["Lukmund","...I see. Even without the Legacy's support, you can still use brainwaves to control your ST to a degree."],["Lukmund","It's truly a pity that someone of your talent can no longer be of use to me."],["","Apophis resumes its combat stance, with its head monitor tightly locked onto Lukmund."],["QRF Captain","Your Excellency, watch out!"],["","Sensing the urgency of the situation, the DLAF officer crashes his ST into Apophis at high speed, thwarting Phoenix's attack at the last moment."],["QRF Captain","We'll handle this. Please retreat!"]],"441406301":[["","Eastern Parill Desert"],["Grant","These guys don't know when to give up! They've been on our tail for almost an hour!"],["Dana","Fortunately, they're not that fast. As long as our path isn't cut off, we won't be caught."],["Dana","The problem is we can't get in touch with Kaidan. Could it be that they..."],["Grant","Pfft, no way, that's the boss you're talking about. It's not that easy to take him down."],["Grant","...Perhaps he just can't initiate active communications for some reason."],["???","As Vesper's front line has fully retracted, the DLAF have regained electromagnetic superiority."],["???","If they respond now, they'll be immediately targeted by the DL's retaliation."],["Dana","...And you are?"],["???","Oh, sorry, I forgot to take off this silly outfit."],["Anderson","I hope you still remember me."],["Grant","Anderson? What are you doing here!?"],["Anderson","I'm here to guide you to the secret safe house."],["Dana","...And which side's safe house are you referring to?"],["Anderson","I see, a reasonable degree of vigilance. It seems my self-introduction wasn't thorough enough."],["Anderson","Senior Agent Smiths Anderson of the General Security Administration, codename \"A,\" assigned by Madam Rosemary to assist GKD."],["Anderson","Now, are you willing to try trusting me?"],["","Parill Desert Periphery and Central Mining Area Border"],["Kaidan","Sorry for dragging you out of there, Dr. Elise."],["Elise","...No."],["Elise","You were right... If we had stayed there, it would only have allowed Lukmund's conspiracy to fully succeed..."],["","*beep-beep*"],["","The ST's warning system suddenly sounds an alarm, and Kaidan notices multiple DL ST signals approaching from various directions."],["Kaidan","Damn, are those DL pursuers?!"],["","The path forward is blocked, and the only option is to break through at full speed until they are discovered. Settling on this plan, Kaidan loads the last magazine into his shotgun."],["","Wait, Kaidan Newman."],["","Two STs rapidly approach from behind, ignoring Kaidan and Elise, and heading toward the DL forces."],["","Kaidan recognizes the leading two STs, their external armor covered with scars from recent battles."],["Matilda","27th Mobile Squad, you've strayed from the front line."],["DL Soldier","Major Rossi? A drone detected a possible intruder signal, so we—"],["Hardaway","That was a decoy device prepared by the intruders. Their goal is to lure you away from your position and destroy the defense line."],["Matilda","This is a critical moment for the Vesper offensive. The front line needs you. Don't lose sight of the bigger picture."],["DL Soldier","U-Understood! Sorry, Major, we were too hasty. The 27th Mobile Squad will return to the front line immediately!"],["","The DL ST squad does not dare disobey the officer's orders and immediately changes direction, heading toward the southwest corner of the mining area."],["","It isn't until the DL forces completely disappear from radar range that Matilda and Hardaway turn around and approach the place Kaidan and Elise have hidden."],["Kaidan","Stop! If you come any closer, I'll shoot."],["Matilda","Don't worry, we're not here to fight."],["Hardaway","Erisa Shinohara provided us with some information, but we cannot verify it with our current data alone."],["Hardaway","Therefore, we hope to get some answers from you."],["Matilda","You must have made contact with Vesper's leader already. What are you doing here?"],["Matilda","Ten minutes ago, Vesper launched a concentrated attack in the direction of a demilitarized zone. Was this related to you in any way?"],["Matilda","The Oceanic Conclave... No, what is Governor Lukmund really plotting?"],["Kaidan","...Why are you asking us all this?"],["Matilda","Based on your answers, perhaps we can draw a conclusion—"],["Matilda","Perhaps we can identify who the DL's true enemy really is."],["","XC 119, Evening of March 3, Southern Central Mining Area, DL Operations Command Hub"],["","Vesper's front line has completely retracted to the vicinity of the central stronghold, and the anticipated second wave of EMP bombings has yet to occur."],["","Although the infiltration operation inside the stronghold failed due to the intruders' interference, the DLAF ultimately gained the upper hand on the front. Victory is undoubtedly just a matter of time."],["","With no need for frequent command adjustments, the tense atmosphere in the war room has finally eased."],["DLAF Comms Officer","Rear Admiral, the location of the Vesper firepower concentration has been identified. It's in the old mine admin block southwest of the mining district."],["DLAF Comms Officer","The target seems to be a rapid response unit executing a special mission there, but the specific casualties are unknown."],["DLAF Comms Officer","It's strange, though. Why would a rapid response unit be sent to such a desolate place for a mission..."],["DLAF Comms Officer","...Uh, Rear Admiral? Are you listening?"],["","Tiphys remains silent, staring intently at the tactical tablet."],["","As the communications officer tries to change the subject, a commotion erupts outside the command hub."],["","A group of men in suits barge in, and almost all the soldiers sneer instantly. They are all too familiar with these types—and they loathe them."],["Tactical Intelligence Officer","...What brings agents of the Oversight Committee to the command center?"],["","The agents ignore the soldiers' hostile stares and walk straight toward Tiphys."],["","Several soldiers rise from their seats, blocking the way."],["Tactical Intelligence Officer","If you can't explain your purpose, leave here immediately!"],["","The agents have no choice but to stop and show the soldiers the official orders issued not long ago."],["DL Agent","...Rear Admiral Tiphys Mill, the Oceanic Conclave suspects you of treason. Please come with us."],["","The command center falls into silence, then erupts in anger. Soldiers draw their weapons and level them at the agents."],["DLAF Comms Officer","Are you kidding me!? Rear Admiral Tiphys committing treason? Are you insane!?"],["DL Agent","Our rapid response team has confirmed that the leader of Vesper is none other than Lieutenant Phoenix Mill, formerly of the Strategic Support Forces."],["DL Agent","There is substantial evidence indicating that he has been conducting various acts of terrorism against the DL with the assistance of Rear Admiral Tiphys."],["DL Agent","Just ten minutes ago, Phoenix Mill even attempted to assassinate Governor Lukmund, but fortunately failed."],["DL Agent","He has been eliminated by the Governor himself."],["","Tiphys suddenly raises his head, staring intently at the leading agent, his face full of astonishment."],["Tiphys","...Excuse me?"],["DL Agent","Governor Lukmund has submitted the battle record to the Oceanic Conclave. The above content is confirmed to be accurate."],["","The agent bypasses the soldiers and approaches Tiphys, handing the arrest warrant to him. This time, no one dares to stop him."],["DL Agent","I will repeat this just once more, Rear Admiral Tiphys Mill, the Oceanic Conclave suspects you of treason. Please come with us."],["","Tiphys takes the arrest warrant without even looking at its contents."],["","His gaze unconsciously falls on the watch on his left wrist, which had stopped working at some point."],["","The hands, which were originally a few minutes ahead, had now fallen out of time."]],"441451101":[["","XC 119, March 4, Eastern Parill Desert Region"],["Anderson","Attention, a small DL drone is passing 2,000 meters ahead."],["Anderson","That type is only equipped with the most basic reconnaissance module, so as long as you slow down and remain concealed, you won't be detected."],["Anderson","Soon it will move south, and then you'll have a window of nearly five minutes to pass through."],["Grant","Hey, how do you even know the DL's drone patrol routes so well?"],["Anderson","Our new partner has already infiltrated DL territory in advance and completed a preliminary investigation."],["Anderson","All you need to do is successfully approach the designated rendezvous point. She will assist you in withdrawing to a safe location."],["Dana","A new partner? I thought you'd be making a personal appearance."],["Anderson","Unfortunately, I must stay in Sankara to ensure the safety of Madam Rosemary and Senator Arnold."],["Anderson","Free Milkhama's current stance is unclear. While they show willingness to cooperate with us, they have also reached some sort of agreement with the DL."],["Anderson","It could be that, when Vesper falls, the situation in Sankara will undergo an unprecedented shift."],["Grant","...It's only taken a few days, but the balance that's held here for twenty years has almost completely gone to hell."],["Dana","I'm worried about Kaidan and the others. If they're still within DL territory, their situation will only become more dangerous."],["Anderson","I understand your concerns. We've been trying to track the whereabouts of Kaidan Newman and Dr. Elise."],["Anderson","According to intercepted communications, the DLAF currently does not know their whereabouts... This means they're hidden well, which isn't exactly bad news."],["Grant","Don't you worry about the boss. He's got a wild side, but in a crisis he's cool as a cucumber. The one I'm worried about is Dr. Elise."],["Grant","The whole Phoenix situation has hit her hard. If she becomes fixated on seeking revenge against Lukmund, they probably won't be able to hide out for long."],["Anderson","That's why you should reach the safe house as soon as possible, meet up with the agency's supporters, and share whatever intelligence you have."],["Anderson","In the upcoming operation, agency personnel and other collaborators will be working side by side."]],"441451301":[["","Central Parill Desert, UNCS Territory Secret Safe House"],["","As Dana and Grant enter the safe house, someone is already waiting for them inside."],["Dana","Winston? Is that really you?"],["Winston","Finally. I've been sitting here waiting for you guys for a full hour and a half! I thought I'd been stood up again..."],["Winston","...Where's Kaidan? Why isn't he here? I wanted to ask him what he thinks of the new STs."],["Dana","Kaidan... ran into some trouble and isn't currently with us."],["Grant","Winston, is that new Ursprung model your handiwork?"],["Natalia","Yes, but not entirely. The improvements and adjustments were indeed completed by Dr. Winston, but this doesn't include the Testee Unit at its core."],["Dana","You decided to show up too, Natalia. \"Testee Unit\"... What exactly does that mean? Kaidan mentioned it before, but he doesn't seem to know much either."],["Natalia","Its design originates from Dr. Newman's former friend, a Mr. Harrison."],["Natalia","Although the specific development process is not yet clear, it is certain that it was optimally adapted to the Hyper-Aptamer prototype data from the very beginning of its design."],["Natalia","Based on the combat records from your machine, Kaidan can operate this ST using brainwaves, and without Dive. This should be the reason."],["Winston","...I really can't understand why Harrison, who completed the core neuron nine years ago, kept claiming it was a failed experiment."],["Winston","Back then, he and Newman had a major argument over a certain issue, and shortly after, he withdrew from the Nova-Frame project and all military research into ST Dive development..."],["Winston","It appears they may have conspired in private, choosing this means to stall the research and cloud Blair's judgment."],["Natalia","If not for the confirmation of Kaidan's... Hyper-Aptamer prototype data, we might never have uncovered that this unit was hidden all along in a warehouse on the island."],["Natalia","Fortunately, it's not too late. At least Kaidan has proven in actual combat that this technology has a natural advantage when facing the DL's Bionic Intelligence Frame."],["","At the mention of this point, Winston's eyes light up with excitement."],["Winston","Yes, yes! As long as I can collect Kaidan's new data, I might be able to improve the Testee Unit and achieve a breakthrough in the performance of the Nova-Frame!"],["","Unlike the enthusiastic Winston, Dana frowns."],["Dana","...What is your intent in refining the Nova-Frame? To place it in the military, to wage war against the DL?"],["","Faced with Dana's less-than-friendly skepticism, Natalia remains unfazed, her signature smile still firmly in place."],["Natalia","I won't completely deny the possibility, but that is ultimately a last resort—if all our efforts fail and war unfortunately breaks out."],["Natalia","At this stage, Vesper is retreating due to setbacks in their plans, and the DLAF is slowing down due to Rear Admiral Tiphys's arrest. We still have a chance—"],["Dana","Wait, what did you say? What happened to Rear Admiral Tiphys?"],["Natalia","...An oversight on my part. Although this news is semi-public within the DL, you had no way of knowing, considering your recent situation."],["Natalia","The Oversight Committee has confirmed that the leader of Vesper is indeed Phoenix Mill and suspects that Rear Admiral Tiphys has been providing him with intelligence, indirectly leading to the DL's successive defeats."],["Natalia","The Oceanic Conclave has therefore issued a resolution to temporarily transfer supreme command of the Milkhama Dawnstar League Jurisdiction to Governor Lukmund, who will personally appoint a new frontline commander."],["Natalia","Rear Admiral Tiphys himself is under house arrest, awaiting formal judgment."],["Grant","Lukmund again. Why does it feel like all of this was orchestrated by that creep?"],["Natalia","What's more interesting is that the Oceanic Conclave seems unaware that the Legacy has fallen into Lukmund's hands. Or rather, Lukmund has intentionally concealed this fact."],["Dana","Restricting the DLAF's military actions on one hand, while defying the Oceanic Conclave on the other... What exactly is he trying to achieve?"],["Natalia","His purpose remains unclear, but the planned military actions of the DL will undoubtedly slow down as a result, which presents us with a valuable opportunity."],["Natalia","And whatever Lukmund plans to do with the Legacy, it must be hidden from the eyes of the DLAF and the Oceanic Conclave."],["","Natalia takes out her tactical tablet, taps a few commands, and hands it to Dana."],["","The screen displays a map of East Milkhama, with six special coordinates prominently marked."],["Natalia","These are the six most likely hiding places we have identified. They are all somewhat connected to Lukmund or Ma'at, yet do not belong to any official department of the DL."],["Natalia","To avoid alerting the enemy, we must investigate these locations simultaneously."],["Natalia","This intelligence has been synchronized with Marcus, the Epiphyllum, and Erisa's team. They will cooperate with the Luno Family to infiltrate four of these locations."],["Grant","So that leaves two locations... and you're tossing the whole load our way?"],["Natalia","No, the Madam has arranged for an agent to directly assist with your operation."],["Natalia","Although that agent has some... personality flaws, their abilities as a pilot are beyond reproach."],["Natalia","Especially regarding missions concerning Dr. Newman's Legacy, I believe she will play her part as expected."],["","UNCS Territory, Sunset Valley Military Base, Fourth Hangar"],["","*bang*"],["","A sudden gunshot cracks through the air, startling the guards inside the base. But once they realize the noise came from the fourth hangar, they shrugged it off and resumed their tasks."],["","But inside the hangar, the one closest to the gunshot can no longer remain calm."],["Cicero","C-calm down! You can't blame me for prototype Unit 1 Möbius being stolen!"],["Cicero","Who knew Madam Rosemary would hand over the Testee Unit to that incompetent Winston!? If it weren't for Harrison's technology, how could he have possibly completed the ST improvements before me!?"],["","*bang—bang, bang*"],["","A few more bullets whizz past Cicero's scalp, completely choking off the remaining words in his throat."],["Ophelia","If all you're going to do is make stupid excuses for your failures, I wouldn't mind freeing the UNCS of some academic deadweight."],["","Rage almost consumes Cicero's mind. He wants nothing more than to lash out at the madwoman in front of him—"],["","But in the end, his fury was no match for his fear—he quickly calms down and reorganizes his words."],["Cicero","...The debugging of Prototype Unit 2 has entered its final stage. I rewrote its entire OS myself, aligned with the prototype data—no one else could possibly take over its improvements in such a short time."],["Cicero","Harrison's Testee Unit is ultimately a product of technology from nearly a decade ago, and no matter how much Winston adjusts it, there are sure to be inherent flaws."],["","Ophelia doesn't respond—she just coldly stares at Cicero, with the gun in her hand still drawn."],["Cicero","As long as I can complete the improvement plan for Prototype 2 as scheduled, I can guarantee it will definitely not lose to that Möbius."],["Cicero","You will also definitely not lose to Kaidan Newman!"],["","*bang*"],["","A gunshot rings out once more, but this time the bullet doesn't head toward Cicero. Instead, it accurately hits the tactical board resting on the table ahead, its screen lit with mission commands."],["","Ophelia casually tosses aside the handgun and turns around as if about to leave, allowing Cicero to secretly breathe a sigh of relief."],["Ophelia","Three hours, that's the final deadline."],["Ophelia","If you fail to complete the debugging before the mission starts, then you and this ST will remain here forever."],["","Without paying any attention to the pale-faced Cicero behind her, Ophelia leaves the hangar."]],"422113101":[["Fia","Don't tell me you came unprepared."],["Erisa","We're partners, and partners should support each other, right?"],["Fia","*sigh*...Got it, I'll try to deal with the guards and then find a way to disable the alarm."],["Erisa","It's decided then. I'll handle the rest."],["Fia","I hope all this is worth the risk."]],"422113301":[["Erisa","What is all this?! These guys have got nothing useful at all! I'm so angry...! What a waste of effort!"],["Fia","If anyone should be angry, it should be me. You didn't even do anything."],["Erisa","We're partners, a waste of your time is a waste of my time."],["Fia","And? What's next? You won't get the big news you want from these small fry."],["Erisa","Looks like we'll have to target GKD Parcel Service. I've realized that wherever they go, trouble follows!"]],"422134101":[["Grant","Hey, girl. Long time no see."],["Seven","Huh, what are you doing here, old man? Aren't you supposed to be on a mission with Kaidan? Don't tell me..."],["Grant","What's with that look?! I'm not slacking off! I took a big job transporting STs; I'm just borrowing your hangar to assemble one is all."],["Seven","Oh come on. Don't tell me your \"big job\" is just hauling around these random parts."],["Grant","What would you know?! It's called an industrialized workflow. We assemble it all on site, keeping it efficient. All the big corps do it this way."]],"422134301":[["Grant","Pfft, that was easy. With a password that simple, you may as well have left the door open!"],["Seven","Ah, but let me ask you this—can you activate 10 devices at once?"],["Grant","What is this, a game of Twister? With two arms and two legs, I can only do four at most! Well, maybe if I put on a few more pounds I could just lay flat..."],["Seven","See? But I have my Pochies, so for me it's no big deal."],["Grant","Hey! That actually makes sense!"]],"422117101":[["Camilla","What's the mission this time, Eileen?"],["Eileen","I called you here for something else. Please have a seat."],["Camilla","It's not a mission? Then..."],["Eileen","You must have heard about the great battle that took place in Milkhama recently."],["Eileen","I've obtained more detailed information through Obsidian's internal channels."],["Eileen","I suppose you could say the information has inspired me somewhat... we have a way to further enhance your combat performance!"]],"422117301":[["Eileen","Camilla, how do you feel? Any discomfort?"],["Camilla","I don't know... I can't say—it just feels like my mind suddenly went blank, and then everything in front of me changed..."],["Eileen","..."],["Camilla","It's okay. Speaking of which... this feeling isn't unfamiliar to me at all. It's pretty much the same every time I lose my memory."],["Camilla","At least... At least now I still remember... remember what my goal is."],["Eileen","Thank you for your hard work... Camilla."]]};
